{"id":"n-20261022-xfklnh","category":"tech","display_title":"Publisher Drops Novelist Over AI","display_title_he":"מוציא לאור מפסיק את ההתקשרות עם סופר עקב שימוש ב-AI","short_summary":"Canadian publisher Boréal has severed ties with novelist Thélyson Orélien after an investigation revealed artificial intelligence was used in his novel.","english_level":"C1","words":492,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2026/oct/22/canadian-publisher-boreal-ends-relationship-author-thelyson-orelien-over-ai","title":"Canadian publisher Boréal ends relationship with novelist Thélyson Orélien over alleged use of AI","published_at":"2026-10-22T01:13:01.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-22T01:13:01.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-22T06:15:50.689Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The Canadian publishing house Les Éditions du Boréal has officially severed its professional relationship with the acclaimed Haitian Canadian author Thélyson Orélien. This decisive action follows a comprehensive internal investigation into persistent allegations that the writer utilized artificial intelligence during the creation of his latest novel, C’était ça ou mourir, which translates to It Was Either That or Die.","Intense controversy first surrounded the migration-themed book when it was abruptly withdrawn from consideration for France's highly prestigious Prix Goncourt literary award. This removal occurred after specialized tests conducted with the Pangram artificial intelligence detector indicated a complete, one-hundred-percent probability that the manuscript contained computer-generated text. Initially, the thirty-eight-year-old novelist vehemently denied all accusations, labeling the public claims as slander and heresy, while his Canadian publisher initially elected to stand by him.","However, Boréal announced that subsequent findings necessitated a sharp reversal of that supportive stance. According to the publishing house, working versions and drafts of the novel were gathered and submitted to an independent outside party for rigorous technical analysis. The results of this examination revealed unmistakable traces of artificial intelligence tags embedded deep within the metadata of specific documents. Representatives for Boréal stated that while the exact extent of the technology's involvement remains unclear and may never be fully quantified, the uncovered evidence confirmed that artificial intelligence undoubtedly played a role in the writing process.","Before finalizing the separation, the publisher attempted to collaborate directly with Orélien to gather documentation that might help prove his innocence. That cooperative effort ultimately proved inconclusive. According to the publishing house, the author subsequently informed them that he would refuse to provide any further information or materials regarding the ongoing matter.","Throughout the ordeal, Orélien has maintained a nuanced stance regarding his digital footprint. While speaking to international media outlets and the French newspaper Libération, he insisted that not a single sentence, story structure, or foundational meaning originated from a machine. He clarified that any reliance on technological tools was strictly restricted to background tasks, such as conducting historical research and verifying foreign idioms. The author also shared personal background, noting that he began writing the book in late 2017 on the corner of a table and completed an initial draft of more than three hundred pages in 2019, years before the advent of modern AI services like ChatGPT. Furthermore, the writer fled his native Haiti following the devastating 2010 earthquake that struck the Caribbean island, which was already heavily ravaged by severe poverty and unrest.","In response to entirely separate allegations of plagiarism, Orélien admitted to making unacceptable mistakes in his writing during his early twenties, acknowledging that he was perhaps too impatient without fully understanding how much he still needed to learn. He stressed, however, that admiring someone else's work does not grant the right to claim unowned texts, while insisting his current controversy is a separate issue that has now gone far beyond acceptable limits."],"facts":[{"fact":"Canadian publisher Boréal ended its relationship with novelist Thélyson Orélien following evidence of AI use in his novel C’était ça ou mourir.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Orélien was previously removed from France's Prix Goncourt list after an AI detector indicated a 100% probability of computer-generated text.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Boréal hired an outside party to analyze drafts and found traces of AI tags in document metadata.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Orélien denied using AI to write sentences, stating he only used tools for historical research and foreign idioms.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Orélien previously admitted to making unacceptable mistakes involving plagiarism when he was in his early twenties.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Canadian","lemma":"Canadian","pos":"adjective","he":"קנדי","name":false},{"text":"publishing","lemma":"publishing","pos":"noun","he":"הוצאה לאור","name":false},{"text":"house","lemma":"house","pos":"noun","he":"בית","name":false},{"text":"Les Éditions du Boréal","lemma":"Les Éditions du Boréal","pos":"proper noun","he":"לז אדיסיון דוק בוראל","name":true},{"text":"officially","lemma":"officially","pos":"adverb","he":"באופן רשמי","name":false},{"text":"severed","lemma":"sever","pos":"verb","he":"ניתק","name":false},{"text":"professional","lemma":"professional","pos":"adjective","he":"מקצועי","name":false},{"text":"relationship","lemma":"relationship","pos":"noun","he":"קשר","name":false},{"text":"acclaimed","lemma":"acclaimed","pos":"adjective","he":"מוערך / עטור שבחים","name":false},{"text":"Haitian","lem